[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# City alerts (owner: Miguel)\n\nImports the Câmara do Porto's road-works alerts from the Porto Urban Platform (FIWARE NGSI v2, public, no login) as\nbarriers, so the app avoids them like any report. **They are registered works, not confirmed obstacles**: an alert on\nthe road does not always close the pavement. Say so in the pitch.\n\n- `PortoUrbanPlatform` (REST connector): every 10 minutes, and on any message to `access/city/alerts/fetch`, asks for\n  traffic alerts within 500 m of the demo route (41.1450, -8.6085), latest `validTo` first, 100 at most\n  (24/10: 48 still valid among them). The answer goes to `access/city/alerts/raw`.\n- `CityAlerts` (Python, pure, tests in `tests/test_city_alerts.py`) keeps only active\n  \"Obras particulares\" / \"Obras públicas\" (not \"Cargas e descargas\", events or concrete pumping) and maps each to\n  `{id: \"city-<cmp id>\", kind: \"works\", description: \"Câmara do Porto: …\", lat, lon, reported_at, expires_at, source:\n  \"cm-porto\"}`, with lat/lon the polygon's vertex centroid and `expires_at` its `validTo`. It returns only new or changed\n  barriers, plus each one that left the source, republished with `expires_at` = now (an Action cannot clear a retained\n  message on broker 2.22.0; the app hides expired barriers).\n- `ImportCityAlerts` publishes those retained on `access/barriers/<id>` (QoS 1) and stores what it imported, retained, in\n  the internal topic `access/state/city_alerts` for the next comparison. It is retained, not a `KEEP TOPIC`, so it\n  survives a broker restart together with the barriers (durability is on): otherwise, after a restart, `off` retired\n  nothing and an alert that left the source while the broker was down was never retired. `access/city/alerts/last_ok` / `last_error` (retained)\n  hold the time of the latest import or failed fetch.\n- **On/off switch** (for the demo): retained `access/city/alerts/enabled` = `on` | `off`, QoS 1.\n  `SwitchCityAlerts` on `off` republishes every imported barrier with `expires_at` = now and empties the snapshot;\n  while `off`, `ImportCityAlerts` ignores every fetch (the connector still polls). `on` asks for a fetch at once, which\n  republishes them all. A missing flag counts as `on`. The flag, the barriers and the snapshot are retained, so they survive a broker restart\n  (durability on).\n- The publish loops have no `IF {count} > 0` guard on purpose: `REPEAT` is do-while, so with 0 items `pick` returns\n  `{}` once and the id check skips it. A block that ends with `UNTIL` mis-scopes what follows on broker 2.22.0 (see\n  `AGENTS.md`); with the old guard, an import with no changes published `last_error` instead of `last_ok`.\n\nValhalla accepts 100 exclusion vertices by default (20 barriers); `runtime/valhalla/setup.sh` raises it to 1000."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ROUTE PortoUrbanPlatform WITH TYPE REST_API\n    ADD REST_API_CONFIG\n        WITH BASE_ADDRESS \"https://broker.fiware.urbanplatform.portodigital.pt\"\n        WITH REQUEST_TIMEOUT 20\n    ADD EVENT FetchCityAlerts\n        WITH EVERY 10 MINUTES\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/raw\"\n        WITH METHOD \"GET\"\n        WITH ENDPOINT \"/v2/entities?type=Alert&q=category==traffic&georel=near;maxDistance:500&geometry=point&coords=41.1450,-8.6085&orderBy=!validTo&limit=100&options=keyValues\"\n    ADD EVENT FetchCityAlertsNow\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/fetch\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/raw\"\n        WITH METHOD \"GET\"\n        WITH ENDPOINT \"/v2/entities?type=Alert&q=category==traffic&georel=near;maxDistance:500&geometry=point&coords=41.1450,-8.6085&orderBy=!validTo&limit=100&options=keyValues\""
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION ImportCityAlerts\nON TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/raw\" DO\n    SET \"enabled\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/enabled\" AS STRING\n    IF {enabled} != \"off\" THEN\n        SET \"known\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/state/city_alerts\" AS STRING\n        SET \"now\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"ISO\"\n        SET \"raw\" WITH PAYLOAD AS STRING\n        CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.import_alerts\"\n            WITH ({raw}, {known}, {now})\n            RETURN AS {batch}\n        SET \"ok\" WITH GET JSON \"ok\" IN {batch} AS BOOL\n        SET \"count\" WITH GET JSON \"count\" IN {batch} AS INT\n        IF {ok} EQUALS TRUE THEN\n            SET \"i\" WITH 0\n            REPEAT\n                CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.pick\"\n                    WITH ({batch}, {i})\n                    RETURN AS {barrier}\n                SET \"barrier_id\" WITH GET JSON \"id\" IN {barrier} AS STRING\n                IF {barrier_id} MATCHES REGEX \"^city-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,59}$\" THEN\n                    PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/barriers/\" + {barrier_id} WITH {barrier} WITH RETAIN QOS1\n                SET \"i\" WITH {i} + 1\n            UNTIL {i} >= {count}\n            CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.known_of\"\n                WITH ({batch})\n                RETURN AS {snapshot}\n            PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/state/city_alerts\" WITH {snapshot} WITH RETAIN QOS1\n            PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/last_ok\" WITH {now} WITH RETAIN QOS1\n        ELSE\n            PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/last_error\" WITH {now} WITH RETAIN QOS1"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION SwitchCityAlerts\nON TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/enabled\" DO\n    SET \"state\" WITH PAYLOAD TRIM\n    SET \"now\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"ISO\"\n    IF {state} == \"off\" THEN\n        SET \"known\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/state/city_alerts\" AS STRING\n        CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.retire_all\"\n            WITH ({known}, {now})\n            RETURN AS {batch}\n        SET \"ok\" WITH GET JSON \"ok\" IN {batch} AS BOOL\n        SET \"count\" WITH GET JSON \"count\" IN {batch} AS INT\n        IF {ok} EQUALS TRUE THEN\n            SET \"i\" WITH 0\n            REPEAT\n                CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.pick\"\n                    WITH ({batch}, {i})\n                    RETURN AS {barrier}\n                SET \"barrier_id\" WITH GET JSON \"id\" IN {barrier} AS STRING\n                IF {barrier_id} MATCHES REGEX \"^city-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,59}$\" THEN\n                    PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/barriers/\" + {barrier_id} WITH {barrier} WITH RETAIN QOS1\n                SET \"i\" WITH {i} + 1\n            UNTIL {i} >= {count}\n            CALL PYTHON \"CityAlerts.known_of\"\n                WITH ({batch})\n                RETURN AS {snapshot}\n            PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/state/city_alerts\" WITH {snapshot} WITH RETAIN QOS1\n    ELSE IF {state} == \"on\" THEN\n        PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/fetch\" WITH {now}"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "python",
    "value": "# Script Name: CityAlerts\n\"\"\"Porto Urban Platform (FIWARE NGSI v2) traffic alerts -> barriers of the access/barriers contract.\n\nPure. Functions called from LoT take str arguments and return a JSON str (broker 2.22.0).\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom urllib.parse import unquote\n\nFRACTION = re.compile(r\"\\.(\\d{6})\\d+\")\nSAFE_ID = re.compile(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9_-]\")\nWORKS = (\"obras particulares\", \"obras públicas\", \"obras publicas\")\nNOT_A_BARRIER = (\"cargas e descargas\",)\nMAX_DESCRIPTION = 200\n\n\ndef _parse_time(text):\n    \"\"\"ISO 8601 to an aware UTC datetime, or None. Accepts Z, 2-digit and .NET's 7-digit fractions.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text:\n        return None\n    text = FRACTION.sub(r\".\\1\", text.strip()).replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\").replace(\"z\", \"+00:00\")\n    try:\n        moment = datetime.fromisoformat(text)\n    except ValueError:\n        try:\n            moment = datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z\")\n        except ValueError:\n            return None\n    if moment.tzinfo is None:\n        moment = moment.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    return moment.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef _iso(moment):\n    return moment.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{moment.microsecond // 1000:03d}Z\"\n\n\ndef _points(geometry):\n    \"\"\"Every [lon, lat] pair of a GeoJSON Point / Polygon / MultiPolygon (outer and inner rings alike).\"\"\"\n    coords = geometry.get(\"coordinates\") if isinstance(geometry, dict) else None\n\n    def walk(node):\n        if isinstance(node, list) and len(node) >= 2 and all(isinstance(v, (int, float)) for v in node[:2]):\n            yield node[0], node[1]\n        elif isinstance(node, list):\n            for child in node:\n                yield from walk(child)\n\n    return list(walk(coords))\n\n\ndef _description(text):\n    text = \" \".join(unquote(text or \"\").split())\n    return text if len(text) <= MAX_DESCRIPTION else text[:MAX_DESCRIPTION - 1].rstrip() + \"…\"\n\n\ndef to_barrier(alert, now):\n    \"\"\"The barrier for one alert, or None when it is not active at `now` or not pavement works.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(alert, dict):\n        return None\n    text = _description(alert.get(\"description\"))\n    lowered = text.lower()\n    if not lowered.startswith(WORKS) or any(word in lowered for word in NOT_A_BARRIER):\n        return None\n    valid_from, valid_to = _parse_time(alert.get(\"validFrom\")), _parse_time(alert.get(\"validTo\"))\n    if not valid_to or valid_to <= now or (valid_from and valid_from > now):\n        return None\n    points = _points(alert.get(\"location\"))\n    if not points:\n        return None\n    source_id = SAFE_ID.sub(\"\", str(alert.get(\"id\", \"\")).rsplit(\":\", 1)[-1])\n    if not source_id:\n        return None\n    return {\n        \"id\": f\"city-{source_id}\"[:64],\n        \"kind\": \"works\",\n        \"description\": f\"Câmara do Porto: {text}\",\n        \"lat\": round(sum(p[1] for p in points) / len(points), 6),\n        \"lon\": round(sum(p[0] for p in points) / len(points), 6),\n        \"reported_at\": _iso(valid_from or now),\n        \"expires_at\": _iso(valid_to),\n        \"source\": \"cm-porto\",\n    }\n\n\ndef _retired(barrier, now_moment):\n    \"\"\"The same barrier with expires_at = now: how the broker retires one (it cannot clear a retained message).\"\"\"\n    retired = dict(barrier)\n    retired[\"expires_at\"] = _iso(now_moment)\n    return retired\n\n\ndef _load(text, kind):\n    try:\n        value = json.loads(text) if text else kind()\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return None\n    return value if isinstance(value, kind) else None\n\n\ndef import_alerts(raw_json, known_json, now):\n    \"\"\"Compare a FIWARE answer with the barriers imported last time.\n\n    Returns {\"ok\", \"count\", \"publish\": [barrier, ...], \"known\": {id: barrier}}. `publish` holds the new or changed\n    barriers, plus each previously imported one that left the source, republished with expires_at = now (an Action\n    cannot clear a retained message on broker 2.22.0; the app hides expired barriers). A failed fetch publishes\n    nothing and keeps `known`.\n    \"\"\"\n    known = _load(known_json, dict) or {}\n    now_moment = _parse_time(now)\n    alerts = _load(raw_json, list) if raw_json else None  # an empty answer is a failure, not \"no alerts\"\n    if alerts is None or now_moment is None:\n        return json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"count\": 0, \"publish\": [], \"known\": known})\n    current = {}\n    for alert in alerts:\n        barrier = to_barrier(alert, now_moment)\n        if barrier:\n            current[barrier[\"id\"]] = barrier\n    publish = [b for bid, b in sorted(current.items()) if known.get(bid) != b]\n    publish += [_retired(known[bid], now_moment) for bid in sorted(set(known) - set(current))]\n    return json.dumps({\"ok\": True, \"count\": len(publish), \"publish\": publish, \"known\": current}, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n\ndef retire_all(known_json, now):\n    \"\"\"The \"off\" switch: every barrier imported last time, retired with expires_at = now.\n\n    Same shape as import_alerts, with an empty `known`, so the next import (after \"on\") publishes them all again.\n    \"\"\"\n    known = _load(known_json, dict) or {}\n    now_moment = _parse_time(now)\n    if now_moment is None:\n        return json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"count\": 0, \"publish\": [], \"known\": known})\n    publish = [_retired(known[bid], now_moment) for bid in sorted(known)]\n    return json.dumps({\"ok\": True, \"count\": len(publish), \"publish\": publish, \"known\": {}}, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n\ndef pick(batch_json, index):\n    \"\"\"The barrier at `index` of import_alerts' `publish` list, as JSON (\"{}\" when out of range).\"\"\"\n    batch = _load(batch_json, dict) or {}\n    items = batch.get(\"publish\") or []\n    try:\n        position = int(float(index))\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return \"{}\"\n    return json.dumps(items[position], ensure_ascii=False) if 0 <= position < len(items) else \"{}\"\n\n\ndef known_of(batch_json):\n    \"\"\"import_alerts' `known` map, as JSON: the snapshot to KEEP for the next run.\"\"\"\n    batch = _load(batch_json, dict) or {}\n    return json.dumps(batch.get(\"known\") or {}, ensure_ascii=False)"
  }
]
